{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ובקומה", :translit "u-v'kumah", :gloss "and when she arose"} {:he "נקוד על הוא\"ו", :translit "nequd al ha-vav", :gloss "punctuated on the vav"} {:he "ששכבה עמו קודם ו' שעות וקודם חצות בעוד ששנתו חזק", :translit "she-shakhbah imo kodem v sha'ot v-kodem chatzot b'od she-shenato chazak", :gloss "that she lay with him before six hours and before midnight while his sleep was strong"} {:he "ועל כן לא ידע בקומה", :translit "v'al ken lo yadah b'kumah", :gloss "and therefore he did not know when she arose"} {:he "אבל רות לא שכבה עם בועז אלא לאחר ו' שעות", :translit "aval rut lo shakhbah im bo'az ela l'achar v sha'ot", :gloss "but Ruth did not lie with Boaz except after six hours"} {:he "היינו דכתיב ותקם בטרום יכיר איש את רעהו", :translit "hainu d'katuv v'takom b'terom yakir ish et re'ehu", :gloss "that is what is written: and she rose before a man could recognize his fellow"} {:he "בוי\"ו שלא קמה עד לאחר ו' שעות ע\"כ ידע בקומה", :translit "ba-vav she-lo kamah ad l'achar v sha'ot al ken yadah b'kumah", :gloss "in the vav that she did not rise until after six hours therefore he knew when she arose"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Masoretic accent or vowel point on the vav of ובקומה read as a chronological signal: the event occurred before six hours of the night had elapsed"} {:kind :other, :note "Same principle applied to the vav in ותקם (Ruth 3:14), read inversely: she rose only after six hours had passed"}], :frame {:text "The Ba'al HaTurim reads the night as divided into twelve hours, with midnight (chatzot) falling at the six-hour mark. He links the daughter's act with Lot in Genesis 19:33 to Ruth's lying at the feet of Boaz in Ruth 3:7-14, reading the vav in each narrative as a temporal indicator marking the hour of the night. The verse 'she rose before a man could recognize his fellow' is from Ruth 3:14.", :sources ["Genesis 19:33" "Ruth 3:14"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Masoretic accent or vowel point on the vav of ובקומה read as a chronological signal: the event occurred before six hours of the night had elapsed", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Same principle applied to the vav in ותקם (Ruth 3:14), read inversely: she rose only after six hours had passed", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:06:55.457989954Z", :model "glm-5.2"}